Hi folks,

A little message for the new patch bringing good things like mass unemployment and famine.

[u]Patchnote :[/u]

[list]
[*] Buildings now provide jobs ;
[*] Mass unemployment is now lowering stability ;
[*] Lack of food also lowers stability now ;
[*] The income of the empire depends on the number of employees henceforth, the unemployed bring nothing ;
[*] Production is affected by employment now ;
[*] Addition of a manpower indicator in the planets interface ;
[*] Addition of an indicator of jobs required for buildings ;
[*] Modification of the behavior of the space dedicated to the effects on stability in the tooltips.
[/list]

Hi folks,

A little message for the new patch essentially adding the first version of the planetary stability system.

[u]Patchnote :[/u]

[list]
[*] Added a stability bar to the interface;
[*] Addition of an indication detailing what affects the stability;
[*] The population is no longer capped by the available dwellings. You can be homeless now;
[*] The population can now overconsume food leading to shortages and famines;
[*] A research laboratory has been added for initial colonization;
[*] Population growth is now affected by overpopulation;
[*] Overcrowding negatively affects stability in proportion to the number of homeless people;
[*] The population growth has been reduced by a factor of 1.5 to 1.1 in normal times and 1.01 in the event of overpopulation;
[*] Population retention in famine has been increased from 0.75 to 0.95.
[/list]

Hi folks,

A little message for the new patch bringing some small fixes to planetary production and population management.

[u]Patchnote :[/u]

[list]
[*] Adjustment of the margin at the bottom of the description box ;
[*] Addition of an indication on the population of the selected planet ;
[*] The urban center can now accommodate 10k inhabitants ;
[*] The colonial post and the colonial administration can accommodate 5k inhabitants each ;
[*] The starting planet now starts with 1 administrative center, 1 agricultural industry, 3 mining industries, 1 refinery, 1 power station, 1 civil industry and 1 urban center ;
[*] Colonial post: civilian production increases to 10 and can accommodate 5k inhabitants ;
[*] Colonial administration: civilian production increases to 10 and can accommodate 5k inhabitants ;
[*] Administrative center: no longer produces food, energy or civilian production ;
[*] Administrative city: no longer produces food, energy or civilian production ;
[*] Imperial administration: no longer produces food, energy or civilian production.
[/list]

Hi folks,

A little message for the new patch which touches on quality of life by adding descriptive panels for a better understanding of the interface. For the moment, only the main interface and buildings are concerned.

[u]Patchnote :[/u]

[list]
[*] Addition of description panels;
[*] Addition of icons for civil, space and military productions;
[*] Fixed a bug where it was not possible to select a star near the top of the main interface;
[*] The refinery consumes 2 energies instead of producing 1 now;
[*] Civilian production in civil industry has increased from 100 to 10.
[/list]
